<title>AUSTRALIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>AUSTRALIA GOVERNMENT LIST (970711)</p>
<p> Governor-General (Sworn in 16 Feb 96)...........William DEANE</p>
<p>(appointment terminates 31 Dec 2000)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>LIBERAL-NATIONAL COALITION GOVERNMENT</p>
<p>(Formed 2 Mar 96, sworn in 11 Mar 96)</p>
<p> Prime Minister......John HOWARD</p>
<p> Deputy prime minister..............Tim FISCHER</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Trade)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Communications &amp; Arts...........Richard ALSTON</p>
<p> Defence...........Ian McLACHLAN</p>
<p> Employment, Education &amp; Training..............Amanda VANSTONE</p>
<p> Environment.........Robert HILL</p>
<p> Finance..............John FAHEY</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...............Alexander DOWNER</p>
<p>Health &amp; Family Services....Michael WOOLDRIDGE</p>
<p> Industry, Science &amp; Tourism.........John MOORE</p>
<p> Primary Industries &amp; Energy......John ANDERSON</p>
<p>Social Security..Jocelyn NEWMAN</p>
<p> Trade................See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p>Transport &amp; Regional Development....John SHARP</p>
<p> Treasurer........Peter COSTELLO</p>
<p> Workplace Relations &amp; Small Business..............Peter REITH</p>
<p>				- - - - - -</p>
<p>JUNIOR MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Aboriginal &amp; Torres Strait Islander Affairs.......John HERRON</p>
<p> Administrative Services.............David JULL</p>
<p> Attorney-General................Daryl WILLIAMS</p>
<p> Assistant Treasurer...Jim SHORT</p>
<p> Customs &amp; Consumer Affairs.......Chris ELLISON</p>
<p> Family Services..Bronwyn BISHOP</p>
<p> Immigration, Multicultural Affairs.............Philip RUDDOCK</p>
<p> Resources &amp; Energy...............Warwick PARER</p>
<p> Schools, Vocational Education.......David KEMP</p>
<p> Science &amp; Technology............Peter McGUARAN</p>
<p> Small Business, Consumer Affairs.Geoff PROSSER  Sport, Territories, Local government............Warwick SMITH</p>
<p> Veterans' Affairs...Bruce SCOTT</p>
<p>				- - - - - -</p>
<p> Reserve Bank Governor ..........Ian MACFARLANE</p>
